    "On register-matched text Binoculars clearly beats raw perplexity: zh AUROC 0.63 -> 0.83 and recall at 0 FP 3% -> 43% with the 1.5B pair; en 0.79 -> 0.97.",
    "The larger pair helps: 0.5B gives zh 0.72 / en 0.83, 1.5B gives 0.83 / 0.97.",
    "Across registers the score inverts (Claude proposal vs CSL abstracts AUROC 0.20-0.28): the proposal mixes English citations, tables and Taiwanese usage, which raises both perplexity and the Binoculars ratio. Absolute thresholds must be calibrated per register (local baseline), never reused globally.",
